    id: "ex-react-hydration-mismatch-cause",
    chapter: "react-rendering-strategies",
    level: "advanced",
    title: "Diagnose a hydration mismatch from the snippet",
    brief: "<p>Write <code>diagnoseHydrationCause(code)</code>: given a string of source code, check it against this chapter's table of usual causes, in this priority order, and return the first match — <code>\"new Date()\"</code> or <code>\"Date.now()\"</code> → <code>\"time-dependent value\"</code>; <code>\"Math.random()\"</code> → <code>\"random value\"</code>; <code>\"typeof window\"</code> → <code>\"environment check\"</code>; <code>\"localStorage\"</code> or <code>\"matchMedia\"</code> → <code>\"browser-only API\"</code>. Return <code>\"unknown\"</code> if nothing matches.</p>",
    starter: "function diagnoseHydrationCause(code) {\n  // TODO\n}\n\nconsole.log(diagnoseHydrationCause(\"const id = Math.random();\")); // \"random value\"\n",
    hints: [
      "String.prototype.includes checks for each trigger substring, in the order the brief lists them.",
      "Check the two-substring causes (Date, localStorage/matchMedia) with an ||.",
    ],
    solution: "function diagnoseHydrationCause(code) {\n  if (code.includes(\"new Date()\") || code.includes(\"Date.now()\")) return \"time-dependent value\";\n  if (code.includes(\"Math.random()\")) return \"random value\";\n  if (code.includes(\"typeof window\")) return \"environment check\";\n  if (code.includes(\"localStorage\") || code.includes(\"matchMedia\")) return \"browser-only API\";\n  return \"unknown\";\n}\n",
    tests: [
      { name: "new Date() is a time-dependent value", body: "assert.equal(diagnoseHydrationCause(\"const t = new Date();\"), \"time-dependent value\");" },
      { name: "Date.now() is also a time-dependent value", body: "assert.equal(diagnoseHydrationCause(\"const t = Date.now();\"), \"time-dependent value\");" },
      { name: "Math.random() is a random value", body: "assert.equal(diagnoseHydrationCause(\"const id = Math.random();\"), \"random value\");" },
      { name: "typeof window is an environment check", body: "assert.equal(diagnoseHydrationCause(\"if (typeof window !== \\\"undefined\\\") {}\"), \"environment check\");" },
      { name: "localStorage is a browser-only API", body: "assert.equal(diagnoseHydrationCause(\"const v = localStorage.getItem(\\\"x\\\");\"), \"browser-only API\");" },
      { name: "matchMedia is a browser-only API too", body: "assert.equal(diagnoseHydrationCause(\"window.matchMedia(\\\"(min-width: 600px)\\\")\"), \"browser-only API\");" },
      { name: "unrelated code is unknown", body: "assert.equal(diagnoseHydrationCause(\"return a + b;\"), \"unknown\");" },
      { name: "an empty string is unknown", body: "assert.equal(diagnoseHydrationCause(\"\"), \"unknown\");" },
    ],
