    brief: "<p>Write <code>buildErrorReport(error, info, context)</code>, assembling the report this chapter's <code>onError</code> example sends: <code>{ message, componentStack, route, release, userId }</code>. <code>error</code> is a real <code>Error</code>; <code>info</code> is <code>{ componentStack }</code>; <code>context</code> is <code>{ route, release, session }</code>, where <code>session</code> may be <code>null</code> — never throw when it is, and report <code>userId: null</code> in that case.</p>",
    starter: "function buildErrorReport(error, info, context) {\n  // TODO\n}\n\nconsole.log(buildErrorReport(new Error(\"boom\"), { componentStack: \"in Widget\" }, { route: \"/x\", release: \"1.0\", session: { id: \"u1\" } }));\n// { message: \"boom\", componentStack: \"in Widget\", route: \"/x\", release: \"1.0\", userId: \"u1\" }\n",
